  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It passes the typecheck, but I couldn't run it in a browser, so none of the behaviour has been seen on screen.\n\n- **Model and path:** The soldier loads from `/assets/soldier.glb` and loops `Walk`. Each frame it is placed on a circle of radius 4 around the origin, and its yaw is set to the direction of travel.\n- **Facing:** I assumed the model faces +Z. If it walks backwards or sideways in the browser, the fix is one yaw offset in `placeSoldier`.\n- **Controls:** Pressing `r` crossfades to `Run` over 0.4 s, and `w` crossfades back to `Walk`. The ground speed eases toward 3.6 m/s for run and 1.4 m/s for walk, so the pace changes smoothly with the clip.\n- **Scene:** There is a ground plane and a path ring drawn with two thin cylinders. Lighting is a hemisphere light plus a shadow-casting directional light. The camera is fixed above and behind the circle, so it frames the whole path rather than following the soldier.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set in the first frame callback, which may run just before that frame is actually drawn.\n- **Unchecked sizes:** I didn't check how `primitives.cylinder` interprets `size`, so the path ring may not match radius 4 exactly.\n\n",
